{"agent":"fix-paging","data":{"by":"grok-4.7","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":2,"detail":"`cut_notice` always tells the caller to \"see the rest with --all\", but that flag only raises the limit to `LIST_MAX_LIMIT`, which is already the limit whenever the list is truncated after `--all` or for a phase list (`_UNPAGED` / `_limit`). Given `task list --all` (or `phase list`) whose engine result is `{truncated: true, shown: LIST_MAX_LIMIT, total: LIST_MAX_LIMIT+1, ...}`, the footer still recommends `--all`. Repeating it returns the same page, so a row past the cap (P-schedule, oldest-touched) is still absent and the miss looks like \"no such phase\".","digest":"538b4a88f5c750d4","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/surfaces/commands/viewers_lists.py:cut_notice","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/surfaces/commands/viewers_lists.py:cut_notice"},{"chunk":2,"detail":"CLI `phase` lists now default to `LIST_MAX_LIMIT`, but the tool path still does `int(a.get(\"limit\") or 25)` unless `all` is set. A tool call `{kind: \"phase\"}` (no `limit`, no `all`) therefore still returns 25 of 199, newest-first, so P-schedule stays off the payload. The same call on the CLI returns up to the max. The new `all` branch does not implement the unpaged phase default this change added on the command surface.","digest":"539c0d997ee0ac35","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/surfaces/tools/operations.py:limit","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/surfaces/tools/operations.py:limit"},{"chunk":3,"detail":"`test_all_lifts_the_page_size_for_every_kind_and_phase_is_unpaged` never lists phases. It only checks `VL._limit` returns `LIST_MAX_LIMIT` for kind `\"phase\"`. The bug is a service/CLI slice: `phase list` printed 50 of 199 and a phase past page one vanished. A build that still slices phase rows at 50 (or ignores `_limit`) satisfies this test, so the regression can close Bd515797884 without failing on that input. The match test has the same hole: tasks are newest-first and `T-needle` is added last, so `view_list(..., match=\"needle\", limit=1)` still returns it if match runs after the page cut.","digest":"feebe0de1bc75697","family":"xai","location":"tests/test_list_paging_notice.py:37","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/test_list_paging_notice.py:37"}],"chunks_total":3,"coverage":"3/3 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":21806,"diff_sha":"912c65796bdef271d4808a7c3e2e49f824eb51b2d7a1e5467a55439061241c06","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in $HOME/src/ddflow/.ddflow/worktrees/fix-Bd515797884","diff_stat":{"deletions":1,"files":1,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":110.4,"excluded_bytes":14306,"excluded_files":4,"excluded_paths":["README.md","tests/golden/__snapshots__/test_golden_cli_help.ambr","tests/golden/__snapshots__/test_golden_mcp_tools.ambr","tests/golden/__snapshots__/test_uc_surf_reporting_pin.ambr"],"family":"xai","findings":3,"max_chunk_chars":8000,"model":"grok-4.7","output_digest":"fa86543580d9031c","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-Bd515797884.critic.grok-4.7.20261111T090633Z-f42796b4.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1,2,3],"reviewed_head":"6db2dbcccd57cb903818e696da728cb5aae34caf","reviewed_paths":{"README.md":"100644 1c52ef6c89e7e9479a2c9f9e629326abea7ce719","ddflow/api/viewers.py":"100644 3d2f3d47658edb804fa7a5807400ccb782225328","ddflow/services/viewers.py":"100644 1379298d9e1b8c2696fa66a137b37b4889292a61","ddflow/surfaces/commands/viewers_lists.py":"100644 6316d13fa07a00d8dfb0aa3ee80467487cd3f058","ddflow/surfaces/tools/operations.py":"100644 988effdf11f58898c473eef7f5d2ce0d4a1dae2b","ddflow/templates/prompts/help/viewers.md":"100644 fba514d8706e47619aa1ad29519a6b1f11e5be0b","tests/golden/__snapshots__/test_golden_cli_help.ambr":"100644 1e3ab2a5620fe3b6e533032cb41772bbc0baa928","tests/golden/__snapshots__/test_golden_mcp_tools.ambr":"100644 6e59137f08c44115e43e34277